{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1455","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1455","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1455\",\"parent_revision\":\"bec061437afb0c39bb47bf41ffd595491752399db35015253d6d38758a01a29c\",\"root_revision\":\"bec061437afb0c39bb47bf41ffd595491752399db35015253d6d38758a01a29c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nE2e tests in `test_live_validation.py` create real GitHub issues in the production repo during test runs. The current cleanup mechanism (in-memory issue tracking + PyGithub teardown) has a single point of failure: if teardown is skipped or exceptions occur, orphaned issues remain in the production repo indefinitely. This was observed on 2026-04-03 when 253 orphaned test issues and 1 MCP-TEST orphan were found open in the repo.\\n\\nA dedicated test sandbox repo (`Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills_test_sandbox`) would make it structurally impossible for test issues to appear in the production issue list, regardless of cleanup success or failure.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWithout this, any e2e test cleanup failure contaminates the production issue list. The emergency sweep in CI mitigates this but is reactive, not preventive.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Fix commit: `4aaab5b` on branch `claude/fix-ci-tests-coverage-wDHxJ`\\n- Current mitigations: `try_get_github` mock in unit tests, hardened teardown with logging, CI emergency sweep for `[MCP-TEST-*]` issues\\n- Prior incident: 254 orphaned issues closed on 2026-04-03\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Is Broken Or Missing\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- E2e tests create real GitHub issues in `Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` (production)\\n- No structural isolation between test-created issues and real issues\\n- Cleanup depends on in-memory state that is lost if the process crashes\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Success Looks Like\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- A private repo `Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills_test_sandbox` exists for test use\\n- `backlog_core` supports a `BACKLOG_TEST_REPO` env var that overrides `discover_repo()`\\n- The `test-e2e` CI job sets `BACKLOG_TEST_REPO` so all test issues land in the sandbox\\n- Production repo never receives test-created issues\\n</div>\\n\\n## Verbatim User Report\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCreate test sandbox repo for e2e test isolation\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"361bfa16706575ae1e136627ba98e7f575225a9ca0d8f893511af3cb95368897\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWFYoQ\"}"}